{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And he blessed Joseph and said</b> — the reason is that in his love for Joseph he blessed his sons, signifying that Joseph had no other offspring and all his blessing lay in the blessing of these youths. Or, his other sons would be named after their brothers and from their blessing they too would be blessed — and this is the correct interpretation in my eyes, for the prophet says (Genesis 48:6), \"and your offspring that you beget after them shall be yours,\" and his word would not be in vain, but he did beget sons after them, according to the opinion of Onkelos, who said, \"and sons whom you beget after them,\" and \"that you begot (אֲשֶׁר הוֹלַדְתָּ)\" would be past tense in place of future, like \"which I took from the hand of the Amorite (אֲשֶׁר לָקַחְתִּי)\" (Genesis 48:22), and many others besides it. For according to the plain sense it would appear that he already had sons whom he begot after his coming down to Egypt, from the fact that it was necessary to elaborate and not say: 'And now, your two sons born to you, Ephraim and Manasseh, shall be mine like Reuben and Simeon, and your offspring that you beget shall be yours.' And this is the reason for what it says (Genesis 41:50), \"And to Joseph were born two sons before the year of famine came,\" for after the famine other sons were born to him, and Scripture does not mention them because there is no need:" "<b>The Elohim before whom my fathers walked, Abraham and Isaac</b> — the prophet calls upon the Elohim of his fathers, who possesses greatness and might and performed for them great and awesome deeds, and he calls upon the El of truth who has been his shepherd from his beginning. And it is possible that \"הָרֹעֶה אֹתִי\" (my shepherd) is from the stem of \"רֵעֲךָ וְרֵעַ אָבִיךָ אַל תַּעֲזֹב\" (Proverbs 27:10), for in that attribute there is peace and friendship, and \"the angel who redeems me\" is the one who answers him in the time of his distress, who said to him, \"I am the El of Bethel\" (Genesis 31:13), and of whom it is said, \"for My name is within him\" (Exodus 23:21), and therefore he said, \"in the midst of the earth,\" and this is clarified for the enlightened. And let it not trouble him — \"from my beginning until this day\" — in light of what we have written on the verse \"and he offered sacrifices to the Elohim of his father Isaac\" (Genesis 46:1), for from his beginning He guided him on the path of truth, but the attribute was not singled out for him until his return to the land of his fathers, because he was outside the land, and also because he needed to conduct himself with Laban in a way of crookedness, which is not the way of truth:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {0 "The verse quoted as Genesis 46:1 in the parenthetical actually belongs to comment index 1; here the citation from Genesis 48:22 is embedded mid-argument."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:46:40.174923105Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}